      "payload": {
        "chunks": [
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_structure_event",
            "content": "In connection with the acquisition of Xilinx, the Company assumed $1.5 billion in aggregate principal of Xilinx's 2.950% Notes and 2.375% Notes (together, the Assumed Xilinx Notes) which were recorded at fair value as of the Xilinx Acquisition Date. The Assumed Xilinx Notes are general unsecured senior obligations of the Company with semi-annual fixed interest payments due on June 1 and December 1.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Assumed Xilinx Notes ($1.5B)",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalStructureEvent",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-31",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_structure_event",
            "content": "On June 9, 2022, the Company issued $1.0 billion in aggregate principal amount of 3.924% Notes and 4.393% Notes. The 3.924% Notes and 4.393% Notes are general unsecured senior obligations of the Company. The interest is payable semi-annually on June 1 and December 1 of each year, commencing on December 1, 2022.",
            "entity_name": "AMD June 2022 Senior Notes ($1.0B)",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalStructureEvent",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-31",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_structure_event",
            "content": "The Company has $3.0 billion available under a revolving credit agreement, as amended, that expires on April 29, 2027 (Revolving Credit Agreement). As of December 30, 2023 and December 31, 2022, the Company had no outstanding borrowings under the Revolving Credit Agreement.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Revolving Credit Facility ($3.0B)",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalStructureEvent",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-31",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_structure_event",
            "content": "On November 3, 2022, the Company established a commercial paper program, under which the Company may issue unsecured commercial paper notes up to a maximum principal amount outstanding at any time of $3 billion with a maturity of up to 397 days from the date of issue. During 2023 and 2022, the Company did not issue any commercial paper under the program and as of December 30, 2023, the Company had no commercial paper outstanding.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Commercial Paper Program ($3B)",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalStructureEvent",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-31",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_return",
            "content": "The Company has an approved stock repurchase program authorizing repurchases of up to $12 billion of the Company's common stock (Repurchase Program). As of December 30, 2023, $5.6 billion remained available for future stock repurchases under this program. This Repurchase Program does not obligate the Company to acquire any common stock, has no termination date and may be suspended or discontinued at any time.",
            "entity_name": "AMD $12B Stock Repurchase Authorization",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalReturn",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-31",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_return",
            "content": "During the year ended December 30, 2023, the Company repurchased 9.7 million shares of its common stock under the Repurchase Program for $985 million.",
            "entity_name": "AMD FY2023 Stock Repurchases ($985M)",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalReturn",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-31",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "legal_proceeding",
            "content": "The Company is named as a responsible party on Superfund clean-up orders for three sites in Sunnyvale, California that are on the National Priorities List. Since 1981, the Company has discovered hazardous material releases to the groundwater from former underground tanks and proceeded to investigate and conduct remediation at these three sites. The chemicals released into the groundwater were commonly used in the semiconductor industry in the United States in the wafer fabrication process prior to 1979.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Sunnyvale Superfund Environmental Proceedings",
            "entity_type_entity": "LegalProceeding",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-31",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "legal_proceeding",
            "content": "To address anticipated future remediation costs under the orders, the Company has computed and recorded an estimated environmental liability of approximately $4.8 million and has not recorded any potential insurance recoveries in determining the estimated costs of the cleanup. The progress of future remediation efforts cannot be predicted with certainty and these costs may change.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Sunnyvale Superfund Environmental Proceedings",
            "entity_type_entity": "LegalProceeding",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-31",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "esg_commitment",
            "content": "The Revolving Credit Agreement also contains a sustainability-linked pricing component which provides for interest rate and facility fee reductions or increases based on the Company meeting or missing targets related to environmental sustainability, specifically greenhouse gas emissions.",
            "entity_name": "AMD Sustainability-Linked Revolving Credit GHG Pricing",
            "entity_type_entity": "ESGCommitment",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-31",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "On May 18, 2023, the Company's stockholders approved the AMD 2023 Equity Incentive Plan (the 2023 Plan), which supersedes the AMD 2004 Equity Incentive Plan and the Xilinx, Inc. 2007 Equity Incentive Plan (the Prior Plans). Under the 2023 Plan, 87,645,874 shares of the Company's common stock are reserved and available for delivery pursuant to awards granted under the 2023 Plan.",
            "entity_name": "AMD 2023 Equity Incentive Plan Adoption",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-31",
            "valid_until": null
          }
        ],
